{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/72663-land-and-domain","id":72663,"title":"Land and Domain","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-02-15T09:27:09-08:00","id":72663,"title":"Land and Domain","content":"Reading the Fear Maker's Promise there is mention of a forgotten contract line of Land and Domain. I thought I'd give a shot of fleshing out the line of clauses. Looking for feedback, especially on power level and catches. Let me know what you think.<br /> <br /> <u><b>Contracts of Land and Domain</b></u><br /> This contract is old and has mostly forgotten. It dates back to feudal eras where lords and knights protected the serfs living on the land. When selecting this contract the changeling must choose a type of domain that covers a discrete area. Most changelings select either Freehold or city, since this covers the largest area. However, on the small end of the scale this can be your personal domain though by its nature slightly limits the usefulness of the contract. Other examples include neighborhood, gang territory, arts district, downtown area. As a general rule, domains should not extend over more than a ten mile radius. A changeling could possibly affect an entire small county but things like states, and countries are out of the contract\u2019s power.<br /> <br /> 1 Dot <u>Herald\u2019s Sight</u><br /> It used to be the ruling class wore sigils and had coat of arms. Those with the right background could read these clearly and know who the person was, what they did, or who their family was. The symbolism of heraldry has somewhat fallen by the wayside but this clause still allows a changeling to read the subtle signs of power.<br /> Cost: 1 Glamour<br /> Dice Pool: Wyrd + Socialize<br /> Action: Instant<br /> <br /> Catch: The character is wearing something that identifies them as part of the domain<br /> <br /> Dramatic Failure: The character gains incorrect knowledge of courtesies to be rendered. They can look forward to a scene of mistaken identities and faux pas. A -2 penalty is applied to Politics and Socialize rolls.<br /> Failure: No knowledge is gained.<br /> Success: For the remainder of the scene, the character gains instinctive knowledge of the domain\u2019s power structure. When looking at someone (assuming the person is recognizable), they are capable of knowing if that person holds an official position within the domain, what the position is called, and what the proper title of address is (though not the person\u2019s actual name). This information grants a + 2 to Politics and Socialize rolls when dealing with those officials. It should be noted that overlapping domains don't have the same officials. Land and Domain (Freehold) will not tell you who the mayor is, the local mob boss or even president of the Home Owners Association. That would require (City), (Mob territory), or (Neighborhoods), respectively.<br /> Exceptional Success: The contract allows you to recognize those in office even through disguises, masks, and magical transformations<br /> <br /> 2 Dot <u>Lady\u2019s Favor</u><br /> Duels are not as common as they were for conflict resolution. It used to be when disagreements arose between domains champions could be selected to face off against each other to avoid full out battle. Before heading into these clashes, blessing were often given to help sway the outcome. Formal duels are rarely found outside Changeling society but there is still usefulness in this clause.<br /> Cost: 2 Glamour<br /> Dice Pool: Wyrd + Manipulation<br /> Action: Instant<br /> <br /> Catch: Before the start of the competition the character gave their champion something for luck and they are visibly displaying it during the contest<br /> <br /> Dramatic Failure: Same as success but they take the worse of the two rolls.<br /> Failure: Clause fails to activate<br /> Success: The champion is able to chose to reroll one dice pool of his choosing, involving a one on one fight, duel, or contest. They may take the better result. The reroll must be used within one scene or the luck fades.<br /> Exceptional Success: The champion receives bonus dice equal to the changeling's Wyrd on the reroll.<br /> <br /> 3 Dot <u>Edict from the Mountaintop</u><br /> Cost: 2 Glamour + 1 Glamour (optional)<br /> Dice Pool: Wyrd + Presence<br /> Action: Instant<br /> <br /> Catch: Character must proclaim his words loudly from above the highest spot in the domain<br /> <br /> Dramatic Failure: You go hoarse or the very wind snatches up your voice. You gain the mute flaw for one scene.<br /> Failure: Your words falter and fail to be heard.<br /> Success: The character speaks up to three sentences and over the next day all those within the domain receive your proclamation. It may come over the radio, as a phone or text message, internet pop-up ad, or heard in a passing conversation but all will hear it, understand it, and know it\u2019s important. No one is actually compelled to do or respond to the message you\u2019ve sent.<br /> For an additional tithe of one glamour, one sentence can be used as a Mask. The limit still applies but where mortals will hear about the importance of participating in upcoming elections, changelings will hear about where the upcoming Autumn coronation is being held and potential targets for the Ashen Hunt.<br /> Exceptional Success: The changeling can select who does or does not receive the message.<br /> <br /> 4 Dot <u>Fisher King\u2019s Blessing</u><br /> Cost: 3 Glamour and 1 Willpower<br /> Dice Pool: Wyrd + Stamina<br /> Action: Instant<br /> <br /> Catch: The character wastes away as he takes on the burdens and difficulties of his domain. Treat this as a disease that imposes a -2 penalty to all rolls and deals 3 lethal damage every week (Stam+Resolve to resist). It cannot be cured and damage cannot be healed until the clause has run its course.<br /> <br /> Dramatic Failure: Treat the character as having used the catch. If the catch was used, then they automatically fail their first Stam+Resolve roll to resist damage<br /> Failure: Nothing happens.<br /> Success: For every success, one Craft specialty may be selected. For one month, the time it takes to make items within that specialty is halved if crafted within the domain.<br /> Exceptional Success: All rolls dealing with the chosen specialties also receive a +2 dice bonus.<br /> <br /> 5 Dot <u>The Lord\u2019s Protection</u><br /> Now known as the Children\u2019s Contract, the full versatility of this clause has been largely lost. For those that know its full secrets, it\u2019s a power tool against enemies and a boon to those under your protection.<br /> Cost: 5 Glamour and 1 Willpower<br /> Dice Pool: Wyrd + Resolve<br /> Action: Instant<br /> <br /> Catch: A changeling may cast this clause for no glamour cost if they have just witnessed a member of the antagonist group ritualistically torture a member of the protectorate on a seasonal equinox or solstice. Changelings may act as a proxy stand-in for the True Fae when fulfilling this catch.<br /> <br /> Dramatic Failure: The spell backfires. Antagonists gain a +2 bonus to all rolls when interacting with protectorates.<br /> Failure: The ward fails to be established<br /> Success: For one month a powerful warding is set up over the domain. Choose one group as antagonists (examples: True Fae, Hobgoblins, Vampires, Ghouls, the Two Streets Gang, the police) and another as your protectorate (examples: children ages 1-12, teenagers 13-19, Summer Courtiers, Wizened). The antagonists cannot pass into the domain boundaries purposefully. A willpower point may be spent to make an attempt but even then a Resolve+Composure roll must be succeeded. Once inside they suffer a penalty equal to successes rolled when interacting with the protectorates in any way (minimum penalty of -2).<br /> Exceptional Success: The protection lasts till the end of the season. If the catch was fulfilled when the clause was invoked, AND the protectorate group chosen was \u2018children\u2019, AND the antagonist group chosen was 'the True Fae', then an exceptional success allows the option of extending the duration of the ward even further. By sacrificing a willpower DOT, the ward lasts a year and a day.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2290-trickyboots","name":"TrickyBoots","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2290_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-07T13:15:13-08:00","id":86210,"title":"","content":"I love the idea of this-- when I used Fearmaker's Promise, I also thought a lot about the lost contract of Land and Domain. I like the ideas for each of the dot levels, but I'm wondering if they all fit in the same contract group? I like the three and four dot levels as part of the Children's contract, but I envisioned different things for the earlier levels. <br /> <br /> My initial idea was that the first or second level of the Land and Domain contract should be based on the old rituals to prevent evil spirits from entering a home. I was thinking about both the tradition of leaving milk out for the fairies in Celtic traditions and the mark of lambs blood for the angel of death in the tenth plague of Egypt-- essentially offerings left to appease evil spirits. The contract would allow the changeling to leave out an offering to ward a domicile or clearing from Keepers and puppets. Sorry that this comment is a little chaotic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2002-quynce","name":"Quynce","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2002_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"34"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-07T14:41:35-08:00","id":86282,"title":"","content":"Some thoughts:<br /> <br /> Make it require a domain you legitimately have the ability to protect (as defined in old style feudalism), so only Freehold Monarchs can get away with an entire city; the first dot will of course work outside your domain.<br /> <br /> Lady's Favour has nothing to do with domains at all. Maybe a long term but modest bonus (+2) to give to your assistants when serving the domain. Autumn Queen appoints a guard to a particularly bad hedge gate, so long as they're doing that job: +2<br /> <br /> Fisher King's Blessing is a bit arbetary, only affecting Crafts. (Also, Fisher King is already a merit). Why not a powerful scrying ability, the sort of thing that could answer questions like &quot;how many Hedge Gates in my domain?&quot;, obviously it has limits. No tracking down Gentry or Fetches. No tracing down Changelings without beating their roll.<br /> <br /> The Lord's Protection is good, but the True Fae would have no trouble beating it. Bump up the Resolve + Composure roll to need to beet the changelings successes, and also mention that half it's effectiveness is that you don't need to outrun the lion, only the slowest zebra.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}